    "narrative": "Ghost Ride the WHIP enters August 17th with a primary objective of chasing stolen bases while balancing game caps, led by our strongest play of the day, **Vinnie Pasquantino** (76.16). He presents our cleanest profile, benefiting from a high-leverage matchup against Barnett and an ideal spot in the five-hole, where his ability to capitalize on SP skill gaps is maximized. **Corbin Carroll** (69.89) remains a high-floor start despite a 30% rain risk; while the platoon disadvantage against Gamboa is suboptimal, his projected utility in the two-hole and raw speed upside keep him as a pillar of our lineup. **Austin Riley** (66.15) also earns a strong recommendation today, as his power-leaning profile is bolstered by Ober\u2019s high-frequency base-stealing allowance, granting us a secondary path to value beyond standard run production.\n\nThe decision to start **Seiya Suzuki** (61.27) over our bench depth was primarily driven by his projected spot in the two-hole against Castillo, L. **Henry Bolte** (51.98) was the most difficult exclusion from the high-tier, falling into the marginal bucket due to the neutral nature of his R/R matchup against Wacha. While **Zach McKinstry** (48.85) is currently rostered, he barely maintains his floor status; he is being held in the lineup strictly for his positional versatility and speed profile, though his efficiency is hampered by Mlodzinski\u2019s specific skill set. We are monitoring the weather closely regarding **Gabriel Moreno** (57.78); he remains a marginal start, but should the 30% rain risk materialize into a postponement, we are prepared to pivot to our deeper reserves, provided we can navigate the absences of **Josh Naylor**, **James Wood**, **Tyler Soderstrom**, and **Jose Caballero**, who are currently unavailable due to scheduling or IL status. Future depth pieces like **Mickey Moniak**, **Giancarlo Stanton**, **Trevor Story**, **Brice Turang**, **Isaac Paredes**, **Max Muncy**, **Dalton Rushing**, **Cole Young**, **Edwin Arroyo**, and **Travis Bazzana** remain on standby should our daily efficiency metrics dictate a roster shift.",
